     <text:p text:style-name="P535">[1] National Electrical Manufacturers Association (NEMA), Rosslyn, VA USA. <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis">PS3 / ISO 12052 Digital Imaging and Communications in Medicine (DICOM) Standard</text:span>. <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://www.dicomstandard.org/" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link">https://www.dicomstandard.org/</text:span></text:a> .</text:p>
     <text:p text:style-name="P535">[2] OFFIS e. V., <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis">DCMTK (DICOM Toolkit)</text:span>, <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://dcmtk.org/en/dcmtk/" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link">https://dcmtk.org/en/dcmtk/</text:span></text:a></text:p>
     <text:p text:style-name="P535">[3] Mathieu Malaterre, <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis">GDCM (Grassroots DICOM)</text:span>, <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/gdcm/" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link">https://sourceforge.net/projects/gdcm/</text:span></text:a></text:p>
     <text:p text:style-name="P535">[4] The Qt Company, <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis">Qt</text:span>, <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://www.qt.io/" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link">https://www.qt.io/</text:span></text:a></text:p>
    </text:index-body>
   </text:bibliography>
   <text:h text:style-name="P654" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc35961_4032426435"/>Implementation Model<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc35961_4032426435"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P371">Starviewer is a DICOM viewer that integrates image visualisation and assessment tools for medical image diagnosis, reconstruction techniques, 3D navigation tools and image fusion support. It adds functional modules and it may be integrated with healthcare information systems such as PACS and RIS servers.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P653">This DICOM Conformance Statement covers Starviewer versions 2.0.*.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P653">Starviewer can open and render most DICOM image IODs and encapsulated PDFs, and can generate series of modality OT from screenshots. It supports networking with DIMSE-C and DICOMWeb protocols and printing to DICOM printers.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P653">DICOM support relies on the DCMTK <text:bibliography-mark text:identifier="DCMTK" text:bibliography-type="www" text:address="Escherweg 2, 26121 Oldenburg, Germany" text:author="OFFIS e. V." text:title="DCMTK (DICOM Toolkit)" text:url="https://dcmtk.org/en/dcmtk/">[2]</text:bibliography-mark><text:s/>and GDCM <text:bibliography-mark text:identifier="GDCM" text:bibliography-type="www" text:author="Mathieu Malaterre" text:title="GDCM (Grassroots DICOM)" text:url="https://sourceforge.net/projects/gdcm/">[3]</text:bibliography-mark><text:s/>libraries, except for the DICOMWeb protocols that use a custom implementation relying on HTTP implementation by Qt <text:bibliography-mark text:identifier="Qt" text:bibliography-type="www" text:address="Miestentie 7, 02150 Espoo, Finland" text:author="The Qt Company" text:title="Qt" text:url="https://www.qt.io/">[4]</text:bibliography-mark>.</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_2" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc35969_4032426435"/>Application Entities and Data Flow<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc35969_4032426435"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="First_20_line_20_indent">The network and media interchange application model for <text:span text:style-name="T228">Starviewer</text:span> is shown in Figure <office:annotation office:name="__Annotation__35940_4032426435" loext:resolved="false">
