   <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_2" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc45959_4032426435"/>TCP Port Configuration<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc45959_4032426435"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="First_20_line_20_indent">See Section <text:bookmark-ref text:reference-format="chapter" text:ref-name="__RefHeading___Toc45056_4032426435">6</text:bookmark-ref>. <text:bookmark-ref text:reference-format="text" text:ref-name="__RefHeading___Toc45056_4032426435">Configuration</text:bookmark-ref><text:s/>for information on the usage of ports for DICOM and other protocols. This section contains helpful information for product administrators to configure firewalls, application whitelists, etc.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P653"><office:annotation office:name="__Annotation__45907_4032426435" loext:resolved="false">
     <dc:creator>Autoria desconeguda</dc:creator>
     <dc:date>2024-02-23T17:29:38.229195114</dc:date>
     <text:p text:style-name="P685"><text:span text:style-name="T229"><text:s/></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T229">[It is advised to make sure enough information is provided to support security configuration. For example, for Firewall configuration, list all other non-DICOM ports and/or provide a reference to any other security document that may be useful for the reader.] </text:span></text:p>
    </office:annotation>TODO content<office:annotation-end office:name="__Annotation__45907_4032426435"/></text:p>
